[image: image]
Welcome to PlaceCom Weekly!

Welcome to PlaceCom Weekly, a short and simple newsletter designed to keep
you updated and on track.
[image: image]

We know things can sometimes feel overwhelming with multiple deadlines,
requirements, sessions, and updates happening throughout the semester.
That's where the Weekly comes in.

Every week, we'll bring you: Important deadlines you shouldn't miss,
upcoming sessions & our Saturday Save rescources!
-  PlaceCom Comms History Doc: PlaceCom_CommunicationHistory_PublicDocument
<https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X6RWT3Kgv6CG_nmlnCrrTCsLaQHsvG4DnuW8X_=
qp8sc/edit?usp=3Dsharing>

Please refer to this doc to access all previously communicated details from
both CDO and PlaceCom.

- The Saturday Save:  PlaceCom Analyser  2025-26
<https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yBEg-WJS_snOznwEN59AMf-PezW793xk/view?usp=
=3Dsharing>Find
the most useful PlaceCom resource for this week, here.

Important Updates for CPP

   1.

   Placement Analyser


   -

   The Placement Analyser is now available here
   <https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yBEg-WJS_snOznwEN59AMf-PezW793xk/view?=
usp=3Dsharing>
   .
   -

   It brings together insights from the previous placement cycle, offering
   an overview of companies, roles, sectors, CTCs, and locations to support
   your placement preparation.


   2.

   Live Placement Tracker


   -

   The Live Placement Tracker for the upcoming placement cycle is now
   available here
   <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/14R7mtWQSnQEqQnmk_bZfXBupX_icemC=
Xyzsgy3IWUFo/edit?usp=3Dsharing>
   .
   -

   The tracker will be updated regularly and will allow you to:
   -

      View companies that have been confirmed for the upcoming placement
      cycle.
      -

      Track the status of companies that are currently in conversation with
      the Placement Committee.
      -

   We encourage you to refer to the tracker regularly, as it will serve as
   the primary source for placement updates throughout the season.


   3.

   Internship to PPO Guide


   -

   The Internship to PPO Guide provides guidance on making the most of your
   internship with the aim of securing a PPO.
   -

   You can access the guide here
   <https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G69Nq2Cnc4WdTEDwOGNAtF20uT5hyyQXhxs=
OeuXJL14/edit?usp=3Dsharing>
   .


   4.

   LinkedIn Learning Deadline


   -

   The deadline to complete the first 2 mandatory LinkedIn Learning courses
   is 15th August.
   -

   The deadline to complete all 4 mandatory LinkedIn Learning courses is 30=
th
   August.
   -

   Please note that failure to complete the first 2 courses by 15th August
   will affect your placement enrollment. We encourage you to complete the
   courses well before the deadline.


   5.

   Mock Interviews


   -

   Mock interview slots will take place on Saturdays and Sundays for
   students who have completed their resume review.
   -

   Slots will open every Wednesday at 6:00 PM.


   6.

   Resume Review Slots


   -

   Resume review slots will continue to open every Wednesday at 6:00 PM.
   -

   Slots will continue to be released until the end of August.
   -

   We've noticed that several students have not yet booked their resume
   review sessions. This is a mandatory step in the placement process, and
   you will not be eligible to sit for placements until you have completed
   your resume review.
   -

    Resume review slots will only be released until the end of August, so
   we strongly encourage you to book a slot as soon as possible instead of
   waiting until the last few weeks.


   7.

   Office Hours with PlaceCom


   -

   Office Hours are now available here
   <https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jcYuYgIcVdFrt6E1s7C2Ftm9V8nE9V2f7tO=
S31uKcyg/edit?usp=3Dsharing>
   for students who would like guidance on placement-related queries or
   feedback on their resumes.
   -

   If you are booking an Office Hour for resume feedback, please email your
   resume to the assigned panel member at least 6 hours before your
   scheduled slot so they have sufficient time to review it beforehand.


   8.

   Office Hours with CDO Team


   -

   The Career Prep Team's 1:1 Office Hours are now live and can be booked
   through AMS under Student Support =E2=86=92 Advising Hub: Office Hours =
=E2=86=92 Career
   Prep Program.
   -

   These sessions are intended to help you discuss career goals, explore
   roles, organisations or sectors, review draft resumes, and receive guida=
nce
   on your preparation strategy.
   -

   Please note that these Office Hours are separate from the mandatory
   resume review sessions and mock interviews required as part of the
   placement process. Students are requested to book their slots at least 2=
4
   hours in advance.

For any doubts or support, reach out to us through the PlaceCom Chatroom or
email us at connect.placecom@ashoka.edu.in. We're always just a message
away. =F0=9F=A4=8D

